1
00:00:00,680 --> 00:00:03,090
Hi, my name's Thomas, and I built CapFare.

2
00:00:03,640 --> 00:00:06,250
So let's say you find a flight for 170 euros.

3
00:00:06,700 --> 00:00:09,530
A day later, the same seat costs 260 euros.

4
00:00:09,920 --> 00:00:12,150
Or you book, the next morning it's cheaper.

5
00:00:13,580 --> 00:00:15,440
CapFare locks the price of your flight,

6
00:00:15,440 --> 00:00:17,640
wherever you book. And it runs on NEAR.

7
00:00:19,180 --> 00:00:22,010
The extension recognises the flight on any booking site

8
00:00:22,010 --> 00:00:24,040
and offers to lock a maximum price.

9
00:00:27,780 --> 00:00:30,160
A passkey creates a readable NEAR account.

10
00:00:30,160 --> 00:00:33,030
No seed phrase, no gas, and prepaid credit.

11
00:00:35,380 --> 00:00:38,250
The premium comes from a public formula on-chain.

12
00:00:38,650 --> 00:00:41,380
The maximum payout is locked in the vault first.

13
00:00:43,980 --> 00:00:47,350
Choose the deductible and a lock of three to thirty days.

14
00:00:50,380 --> 00:00:52,450
When the price passes your cap,

15
00:00:52,450 --> 00:00:53,780
you get an alert in the app,

16
00:00:53,780 --> 00:00:55,590
by push or by email.

17
00:00:58,180 --> 00:00:59,700
Claim with the original email.

18
00:00:59,700 --> 00:01:02,630
The payout waits for a live check of the booking

19
00:01:02,630 --> 00:01:05,330
after a day, then it's paid from the vault.

20
00:01:10,780 --> 00:01:14,170
Only the flight, fare and price reach the chain.

21
00:01:14,750 --> 00:01:18,780
Edited emails, reused bookings and other people's bookings are refused.

22
00:01:20,980 --> 00:01:25,470
Just booked? The Drop Guarantee pays if the same flight gets cheaper.

23
00:01:28,180 --> 00:01:30,310
Route cover pays against the cheapest fare,

24
00:01:30,740 --> 00:01:33,810
up to three days either side and from nearby airports.

25
00:01:36,080 --> 00:01:38,200
Up to nine travellers on one policy,

26
00:01:38,200 --> 00:01:39,900
and a return trip bought as one.

27
00:01:42,480 --> 00:01:44,580
Liquidity providers fund two vaults.

28
00:01:45,030 --> 00:01:47,400
Every policy is fully collateralised.

29
00:01:49,480 --> 00:01:53,410
So why NEAR? Gasless meta-transactions through our relayer,

30
00:01:53,820 --> 00:01:55,390
and readable named accounts.

31
00:01:56,060 --> 00:02:01,270
NEP-141 tokens, async cross-contract calls that roll back on failure,

32
00:02:01,700 --> 00:02:05,010
and ed25519 checks on-chain.

33
00:02:05,850 --> 00:02:07,540
All on the public explorer.

34
00:02:09,080 --> 00:02:13,240
It's a testnet prototype: live contracts, demo prices.

35
00:02:14,680 --> 00:02:17,770
So this is CapFare, built for the NEAR Hackathon.
